WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:11.170
If you create a sustainable city,

00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:13.470
a city that has circular principles,

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:16.230
a city that engages with the environment,

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:18.310
you are creating a healthier population.

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:21.050
The problem here is we
haven't made that link

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:25.263
between circular design and livelihoods.

00:00:26.507 --> 00:00:29.690
You know, the Ellen MacArthur
foundation talks about

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:32.050
this idea of circular economy pioneers.

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:36.440
A lot of the things that
I wanted to learn about,

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:37.773
nobody is teaching.

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:43.020
Or, they've only been teaching
it for the past five years.

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:45.950
It's all so new that in a way,

00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:47.360
you couldn't have done it before.

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:51.190
- But then you leave the
footprints for people to follow.

00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:56.150
- Exactly, you are creating that new path.

00:00:56.150 --> 00:00:58.420
This is the reason why people like us

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:00.060
are interested in circular design.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:02.110
It's not just for what it means now,

00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:05.590
but for what it means in 50, 100 years.

00:01:05.590 --> 00:01:07.850
- Yeah, now we have to
create that narrative,

00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:10.630
which makes people appreciate that,

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:15.060
okay, sustainability
is very, very important

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:19.330
to be able to take care
of my children, my family,

00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:20.610
even myself.

00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:22.084
- Yeah.

